WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.352
For categorical variables, a good starting point is frequency.

00:00:04.352 --> 00:00:09.502
Value counts tell us how many observations belong to each category.

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:14.897
Normalized value counts convert those counts into proportions or percentages.

00:00:14.897 --> 00:00:17.926
Run the code and inspect the channel distribution.

00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:24.663
Ask whether one category dominates the data, whether any categories are unexpectedly rare,

00:00:24.663 --> 00:00:27.553
and whether missing values are still present.

00:00:27.553 --> 00:00:34.928
These simple summaries can reveal important information before we create charts or statistical models.

00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:40.323
For example, if ninety-five percent of transactions come from one channel,

00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:47.878
later comparisons across channels may be unstable because the smaller groups contain very few observations.

00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:56.316
Categorical EDA is not complicated, but it gives you important context about the structure and balance of the dataset.
